{
  "wireMagic": "pb3",
  "pens": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wsWinStyles": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wpWinPositions": [ {
  
  } ],
  "events": [ {
    "tStartMs": 1290,
    "dDurationMs": 5340,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "When it comes to landing spacecraft on planets,\nor moons, or back here on earth – Mars sucks."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 6630,
    "dDurationMs": 5299,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "There’s a lower success rate landing on\nMars than on Venus, the moon, the earth, even"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 11929,
    "dDurationMs": 1710,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Saturn’s moon Titan."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 13639,
    "dDurationMs": 4191,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And in large part, this is because Mars’s\natmosphere is in the perfect goldilocks zone"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 17830,
    "dDurationMs": 2260,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of being a total headache."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 20090,
    "dDurationMs": 4760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "On the moon (or an asteroid) you can use lightweight\nspacecraft made essentially out of tinfoil"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 24850,
    "dDurationMs": 3310,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "because there’s no air to cause drag or\npressure or heat."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 28160,
    "dDurationMs": 4480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Essentially, you save weight not having heat\nshields or thick walls, but need to use rockets"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 32640,
    "dDurationMs": 2720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to land in what’s called a “powered descent.”"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 35360,
    "dDurationMs": 5160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "On earth, or Venus, or Titan, there’s enough\nair that you can land largely unpowered, first"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 40520,
    "dDurationMs": 4240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "by slowing down with a heat shield and atmospheric\ndrag, and then with parachutes."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 44760,
    "dDurationMs": 3560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So you use a lot of weight for heat shields\nand walls and parachutes, but don’t need"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 48320,
    "dDurationMs": 2470,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "big rockets or lots of fuel to land."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 50790,
    "dDurationMs": 4520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "However, the air on Mars is literally the\nworst of both worlds – thick enough that"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 55310,
    "dDurationMs": 3720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "you actually have to deal with it with heat\nshields and walls, but thin enough that it"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 59030,
    "dDurationMs": 2940,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "doesn’t help you slow down much and you\nalso need to use rockets."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 61970,
    "dDurationMs": 4280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Mars is simply a challenging place to land\na spacecraft, which is why we’ve tried so"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 66250,
    "dDurationMs": 4490,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "many different and crazy techniques for landing\nthere: we’ve landed landers and rovers using"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 70740,
    "dDurationMs": 5090,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "retrorockets, in inflatable bouncy airbags,\nby being lowered from a hovering sky crane"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 75830,
    "dDurationMs": 5560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "– all of which ALSO used heat shields and\nparachutes and rocket powered descent before"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 81390,
    "dDurationMs": 1500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the last stage of landing."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 82890,
    "dDurationMs": 4100,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And space agencies are testing other crazy\nthings like giant supersonic parachutes and"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 86990,
    "dDurationMs": 3950,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "inflatable innertubes around landers to increase\ntheir surface area and help them slow down"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 90940,
    "dDurationMs": 4289,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "more in the thin air before landing (probably\nstill with rockets, or sky cranes)."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 95229,
    "dDurationMs": 4021,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Yes, you heard that right – it’s possible\nthat when the first humans land on Mars, we"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 99250,
    "dDurationMs": 2940,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "may do so in an inflatable donut."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 102190,
    "dDurationMs": 3539,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Or we’ll just skim at a really low angle\npast the tops of mountains for a really long"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 105729,
    "dDurationMs": 11070,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "time to slow \ndown enough..."
    } ]
  } ]
}
